{
  "dom_id": "question-167217",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "If the company produces fifteen wooden tables in a week, the weekly profit will be $$4\\,050.$ Find an expression for $b$ in terms of $a.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $b=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "In part 1, we found that $p(15)=225a+15b.$ So, we need to solve the equation $225a+15b=4\\,050$ for the parameter $b.$\n\nWe need to isolate the variable $b.$ To do this, we treat $a$ as though it were a constant and apply the addition and multiplication principles as usual.\n\nFirst, we subtract $225a$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}225a+15b & =4\\,050 \\\\ 225a+15b-225a & =4\\,050-225a \\\\ 15b & =4\\,050-225a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $15:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15b & =4\\,050-225a \\\\ \\frac{15b}{15} & =\\frac{4\\,050-225a}{15} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{15}b}{\\cancel{15}} & =\\frac{4\\,050}{15}-\\frac{225a}{15} \\\\ b & =270-15a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $b=270-15a.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [
    {
